{1}{Greetings, citizen.}{Greetings, citizen.}{}{}{}{ }
{2}{Capt. Wheeler told me to come speak with you.}{}{5}{gf2429 1, qu1144 0, qu1145 0, qu1146 0}{15}{ }
{3}{What is going on here?}{}{5}{qu1146 0}{155}{ }
{4}{What be happening here?}{}{-4}{lf1 0}{155}{lf1 1 }
{5}{Capt. Wheeler told me to come speak with you.}{}{5}{gf2429 1, qa1144 1, qb1144 2, qu1145 0, qu1146 0}{15}{lf3 1 }
{6}{Capt. Wheeler told me to come speak with you.}{}{5}{gf2429 1, qa1145 1, qb1145 2, qu1146 0}{15}{lf3 1 }
{7}{I convinced him to escape. He will meet with you later, he said.}{}{5}{gf2433 1, qb1146 3}{197}{gf2432 1, qu1146 4 }
{8}{I failed to convince him to listen to your plan. What can I do?}{}{5}{qu1146 6}{135}{ }
{10}{You were telling me about the situation here?}{}{5}{lf2 1, qu1144 0, qu1145 0}{65}{lf2 0 }
{11}{What were you saying about Mr. Throgg?}{}{5}{lf6 1, qu1144 0, qu1145 0}{95}{lf6 0 }
{12}{I've reconsidered being your emissary. What do I need to do?}{}{5}{lf4 1, qu1144 0, qu1145 0}{115}{lf4 0, qu1146 2 }
{13}{Are you certain there is nothing that can be done to help here?}{}{5}{lf5 1}{185}{lf5 0 }
{14}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{ }
{15}{And why did he tell you that?}{And why did he tell you that?}{}{}{}{ }
{16}{I was defending the rights of the orcs. He was not amused.}{}{5}{}{25}{ }
{25}{Hah! I am sure he wasn't. He believes the orcs aren't fit to live, let alone have any rights. That's what all this is about - all the orcs want is the right to unionize. I am trying to keep this from deteriorating into...well, into what happened last time.}{Hah! I am sure he wasn't. He believes the orcs aren't fit to live, let alone have any rights. That's what all this is about - all the orcs want is the right to unionize. I am trying to keep this from deteriorating into...well, into what happened last time.}{}{}{}{ }
{26}{What happened last time?}{}{5}{}{35}{ }
{35}{It was a massacre! Capt. Wheeler mowed the protesters down with a mechanized gun, it was horrible. I suppose that is why they chose to hold up inside a factory this time instead of protesting in the open. For Wheeler to get inside, he'd have to sacrifice some men, and that would look bad for him.}{It was a massacre! Capt. Wheeler mowed the protesters down with a mechanized gun, it was horrible. I suppose that is why they chose to hold up inside a factory this time instead of protesting in the open. For Wheeler to get inside, he'd have to sacrifice some men, and that would look bad for him.}{}{}{}{gf2428 1 }
{36}{What happened to Wheeler after he killed the protestors?}{}{5}{}{45}{ }
{37}{That is truly distressing.}{}{5}{}{55}{ }
{38}{It is rather brave of the orcs to try this again after that.}{}{5}{}{65}{ }
{44}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{lf2 1 }
{45}{Nothing. Some on the council actually wanted to give him a medal!}{Nothing. Some on the council actually wanted to give him a medal!}{}{}{}{ }
{46}{That's shocking!}{}{5}{}{55}{ }
{55}{Yes, it is. And what is more, I feel it is directly responsible for the situation that has arisen here today.}{Yes, it is. And what is more, I feel it is directly responsible for the situation that has arisen here today.}{}{}{}{ }
{56}{Why is that?}{}{5}{}{65}{ }
{65}{The orcs feel they have to do things like this to draw attention to their plight. They feel they can not effect any change through political ends, when they are seen as expendable beasts. It is all the more the pity, as Mr. Throgg could be just the man we are looking for.}{The orcs feel they have to do things like this to draw attention to their plight. They feel they can not effect any change through political ends, when they are seen as expendable beasts. It is all the more the pity, as Mr. Throgg could be just the man we are looking for.}{}{}{}{ }
{66}{Mr. Throgg? The man you are looking for?}{}{5}{}{75}{ }
{74}{I wish you luck in your endeavor. Good day.}{}{5}{}{0}{ }
{75}{Donn Throgg is the leader of the orcs. Because he has human blood, we can make a case for his rights to unionize before the council. There has never been a case to determine the rights of an half orc under the law. If an half orc can pass for human, they usually "keep their heads down" so that others won't think of them as orcs. And if they look like orcs, well...}{Donn Throgg is the leader of the orcs. Because he has human blood, we can make a case for his rights to unionize before the council. There has never been a case to determine the rights of an half orc under the law. If an half orc can pass for human, they usually "keep their heads down" so that others won't think of them as orcs. And if they look like orcs, well...}{}{}{}{ }
{76}{I see. So Mr. Throgg appears to be human?}{}{5}{}{85}{ }
{85}{He is unique in that his features have a distinctive orcish cast to them, but instead of making him look the dumb brute, it actually gives him somewhat the appearance of a swarthy rogue. And I've never met an half orc with the charisma he has, or near anyone else for that matter.}{He is unique in that his features have a distinctive orcish cast to them, but instead of making him look the dumb brute, it actually gives him somewhat the appearance of a swarthy rogue. And I've never met an half orc with the charisma he has, or near anyone else for that matter.}{}{}{}{ }
{86}{So what can be done to diffuse this situation?}{}{5}{ps12, lf3 0}{95}{ }
{87}{So what can be done to diffuse this situation?}{}{5}{ps-11}{135}{ }
{88}{So what can be done to diffuse this situation?}{}{5}{ps12, lf3 1}{135}{ }
{94}{This is all very fascinating, but I must be leaving.}{}{5}{}{0}{lf6 1 }
{95}{Donn Throgg must be convinced to give up this foolishness and work with us. This way he has chosen leads to death. Captain Wheeler will not let him leave that building alive if given the choice, so the choice must not be his to make. Mr. Throgg needs to slip out in the night to be certain that he may live to fight another day!}{Donn Throgg must be convinced to give up this foolishness and work with us. This way he has chosen leads to death. Captain Wheeler will not let him leave that building alive if given the choice, so the choice must not be his to make. Mr. Throgg needs to slip out in the night to be certain that he may live to fight another day!}{}{}{}{ }
{96}{Why don't you go in there and propose your plan to him?}{}{5}{ra7}{105}{ }
{97}{Why don't you go in there and propose your plan to him?}{}{5}{ra-7}{125}{ }
{104}{Thank you for the invigorating speech, but I must be going.}{}{5}{}{0}{lf6 1 }
{105}{Because, as a councilmember, I represent the establishment which is holding him down. He will not speak with me. An half orc such as yourself, however, could easily gain his ear.}{Because, as a councilmember, I represent the establishment which is holding him down. He will not speak with me. An half orc such as yourself, however, could easily gain his ear.}{}{}{}{ }
{106}{Okay, I will speak with him for you. What do I need to do?}{}{5}{}{115}{qu1146 2 }
{114}{I am not interested in being your emissary. Good day.}{}{5}{}{0}{lf4 1 }
{115}{Simply go in there and propose my plan to him. I am certain he will listen to reason. [He hands you a key.] They've locked themselves inside, but I convinced the owner to give me the key.}{Simply go in there and propose my plan to him. I am certain he will listen to reason. [He hands you a key.] They've locked themselves inside, but I convinced the owner to give me the key.}{}{}{}{in-4418 }
{116}{I will return after I have convinced him.}{}{5}{}{0}{ }
